    "version": 1,
    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify the cluster PKI is healthy on every node.\n\nChecks per node:\n  - Service cert is valid and not expiring within 30 days\n  - VIP (10.10.0.100) is present in the service cert SANs\n    (critical: if VIP is absent, services behind the VIP reject TLS)\n  - CA cert is valid for 30+ days\n  - Ed25519 signing keys are present (identity layer)\n\nThe PKI is the root of security for the entire cluster. A cert that's\nmissing the VIP SAN is the #1 silent failure mode for traffic behind\nthe keepalived VIP (this burned us for 16 hours on nuc \u2014 see session_vip_cert_fix.md).",
